{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1407121-equipment-bonuses-and-weapons","id":1407121,"title":"Equipment bonuses and weapons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-09T05:18:25-07:00","id":1407121,"title":"Equipment bonuses and weapons","content":"So i have seen several people ask the question but cannot find any responses, how do equipment bonuses interact with weapons. Would the Fate Monkeys Paw spell add dice too using a knife for instance? would it be as dice, or damage if it did. How would it interact with something you dont tend too roll for like armor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6947-cubleds","name":"cubleds","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T20:03:18-07:00","id":1407218,"title":"","content":"I'm not 100% certain how things would interact in 2e but with 1e your weapon rating was an equipment bonus and not automatic damage. So, I'd lean personally to an equipment bonus enhancement on a weapon generally adding to its weapon rating instead of adding to the dicepool.<br /> That said however, I can understand why some spells it fits better for it to just add a bonus to the dicepool instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T21:07:03-07:00","id":1407229,"title":"","content":"What confuses me is that The Right Tool (SoS) and Monkey's Paw (core) apparently do the same thing, or is there something I am missing ? The only distinction I see is that The Right Tool can work on items unsuited for the task (like conducting a delicate operation with a gum wrapper). For weapons, I think this means a flat bonus to the damage done. In theory this could make a sling as deadly as a sniper rifle or a fork as damaging as a chainsaw.<br /> <br /> Normally the accuracy is entirely up to the user (barring any kind of automatic targeting technology or supernatural interference), so it is assumed they are the target. For Fate spells that would require the Reach effect of Monkey's Paw (but oddly enough not The Right Tool) or a separate blessing on the user or an AoE blessing centered on the tool, that way it would envelop the user.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T21:26:37-07:00","id":1407231,"title":"","content":"in Hurt Locker there is a weapon tag for accuracy that adds +1 die bonus too hit, as well as inaccurate giving a -1. Only inaccurate seems too be used, (on a few improvised weapons like a chainsaw). So there is at least one example of die bonuses and penalties on equipment but its rather minor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6947-cubleds","name":"cubleds","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T02:47:40-07:00","id":1407255,"title":"","content":"Damage modifier <i>is</i> the equipment bonus of weapons, so anything which increases equipment bonuses increases the damage.<br /> Armour does not have equipment bonuses because they're not rolled.<br /> <br /> Accuracy/inaccuracy modifiers are additional modifiers that may apply. They are not considered an equipment bonus even if they do function similarly. Likewise, spells that would instead grant bonus dice rather than increase an equipment bonus would also increase the dice pool of attacks instead of the damage.<br /> The exception is if the accuracy bonus comes from an accessory (like a scope on a rifle), in which case that dice bonus is the accessory's equipment bonus (but not the weapon's).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 08-10-2020, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T15:46:55-07:00","id":1407390,"title":"","content":"That does make sense, the annoying part is that there are spells that say they boost equipment bonuses or damage, where as others only list equipment bonuses. This is not me disagreeing with you, more just listing things that cause me confusion on how the rules were meant too be read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6947-cubleds","name":"cubleds","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T18:07:37-07:00","id":1407406,"title":"","content":"Instead of making a new thread, I think my question could be answered in this thread....hopefully.... What bout structures and throws? I mean what's the point of throwing someone threw a window (closed window) or slam them into a wall, besides that it's basically a action movie stereotype?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}